                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To provide with a gore."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "778632a3-1196-4fb5-aac4-a36a95a1c484",
                                                "sense_id": "566f9be3-93dc-377b-a7e6-fb5eb89d4465",
                                                "text": "to gore an apron"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c48f2bc-0178-45ca-999a-bbd11ff51c49",
                                                "sense_id": "566f9be3-93dc-377b-a7e6-fb5eb89d4465",
                                                "text": "If Miss McFlimsey has neat ankles, she can wear short dresses: if she has clumsy ones she can wear a trail; if she is inclined to be (pardon the word) “scrawny,” she can indulge in expensive skirts and protuberant “panniers;” if inclined to embonpoint, she can discard these and “gore” her robes; if her neck and arms are exquisitely moulded, she can undrape their dazzling charms; if bone predominates over plumpitude, she can cover them from the gaze of flying eyes; if she has a disease of the spine, she need not sport “the Grecian bend;” if she is unfortunately healthy, she can call in the aid of that modern deformity—and so on, ad infinitum and ad nauseum.^([sic])"
